/-!
# Finite free étale charts with a power-containing ideal lift

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0813, `lemma-push-ideal`, the monic quotient chart and
numerator generators with the prescribed power adjoined
(blueprint: lem-trf-etale-chart-ideal-lift).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace Algebra

/-- An étale algebra has, near each prime, a principal-localization chart of a monic
polynomial quotient, together with numerator lifts of a given finite list of ideal generators.
Adjoining the prescribed scalar power to those numerators does not change the localized ideal,
and that power annihilates the quotient by the lifted ideal.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0813, `lemma-push-ideal`, proof
(blueprint: lem-trf-etale-chart-ideal-lift).

Proof plan:
1. Apply `Algebra.IsEtaleAt.exists_isStandardEtale` (lem-weil-pbc-etale-locally-standard)
   to obtain `g` outside `q` and a standard étale presentation with monic polynomial `f`.
2. Identify its two-variable quotient with the localization of `AdjoinRoot f` at the
   image `h` of the other polynomial. The maps send `T` to its class and the inverse
   variable to `1/h`; the inverse sends `P/h^e` to `P(T)Y^e`. This gives `θ`.
3. The localization `B_g` is an open subscheme of `Spec B`
   (lem-weil-pbc-principal-localization-open-immersion). Restrict the given étale map
   (lem-a1-etale-open-restriction) and transport it across `θ` to obtain étaleness of `C_h`.
4. The monic quotient has the basis of powers of its root, by `AdjoinRoot.powerBasis'`
   (lem-weil-pbc-monic-quotient-free).
5. Express each `θ(j_i/1)` as `c_i/h^(e_i)` using the fraction description of localization
   (def-weil-ring-localization-away). Set `K` to the ideal generated by the `c_i` and `a_C^m`;
   its displayed finite list of generators proves finite generation.
6. Multiplying or dividing by the unit `h^(e_i)` shows that the localized numerator ideal
   is `θ(JB_g)`. Express `a_B^m` as a linear combination of the `j_i` and apply the
   A-algebra map `θ`: the image `a_C^m/1` already lies in that ideal. Thus adjoining it
   does not change the localized ideal. Since `a_C^m` belongs to `K`, it kills every
   element of `C/K`. These arguments also cover the empty generating list and `K = ⊤`.
-/
theorem exists_etale_chart_ideal_lift
    {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (hEtale : AlgebraicGeometry.Etale
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))))
    (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime] (a : A) (m : ℕ) (hm : 1 ≤ m)
    (r : ℕ) (j : Fin r → B) (J : Ideal B)
    (hJ : Ideal.span (Set.range j) = J) (ha : algebraMap A B a ^ m ∈ J) :
    ∃ g : B, g ∉ q ∧ ∃ f : Polynomial A, f.Monic ∧
      ∃ (h : AdjoinRoot f) (θ : Localization.Away g ≃ₐ[A] Localization.Away h),
        AlgebraicGeometry.Etale (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.map
          (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away h)))) ∧
        (∃ b : Module.Basis (Fin f.natDegree) A (AdjoinRoot f),
          ∀ i : Fin f.natDegree, b i = AdjoinRoot.root f ^ (i : ℕ)) ∧
        ∃ (c : Fin r → AdjoinRoot f) (e : Fin r → ℕ),
          (∀ i : Fin r, θ (algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) (j i)) =
            IsLocalization.mk' (M := Submonoid.powers h) (Localization.Away h) (c i)
              ⟨h ^ e i, ⟨e i, rfl⟩⟩) ∧
          ∃ K : Ideal (AdjoinRoot f),
            K = Ideal.span (Set.range c ∪ {algebraMap A (AdjoinRoot f) a ^ m}) ∧
            K.FG ∧
            Ideal.map (algebraMap (AdjoinRoot f) (Localization.Away h)) K =
              Ideal.map θ.toRingHom
                (Ideal.map (algebraMap B (Localization.Away g)) J) ∧
            ∀ z : AdjoinRoot f ⧸ K,
              Ideal.Quotient.mk K (algebraMap A (AdjoinRoot f) a ^ m) * z = 0 := by
  sorry

end Algebra
